                <pb facs="0527" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.01/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-05T14:00:00-05:00">November 5, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>130. President Machado informed me that Cuba desired to follow the United States
                    in its policy and any future action regarding recognition of the Brazilian
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
